              "text": "LayerNorm is row-wise over N=4096. With 512 threads/block, each thread handles 4096/512=8 elements \u2014 enough arithmetic intensity to hide memory latency while keeping 2 blocks/SM (512*2=1024 \u2264 max_threads_per_block=1024). This is the canonical sweet-spot for a reduce of this width on Ampere.",
